//? Title: DETR tensor bipartite matching and learned object queries
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Check tensor Hungarian assignment against exhaustive solutions, set-loss derivatives and the full transformer graph, then explicitly fit the complete compact source DETR with independent auxiliary matching, paired BN checkpoints and real digit scenes.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.6_object_detection/detr.cpp`.

> The method

DETR predicts a fixed set of learned object queries and trains through a bipartite set objective. Tensor geometry and a rectangular primal/dual assignment solver produce detached targets, while every backbone, transformer and shared-head parameter participates in visible Adam fitting.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/detr_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/detr_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/detr_concept.tikz > build/detr_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/detr_concept.svg build/detr_concept.dvi > build/detr_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
