> Post-norm transformer graph and compact initialization

The backbone emits feature-only ResNet activations. Source2D sine/cosine
positions are tensor-evaluated in Double then cast to model dtype: row encoding
first, column encoding second. Positions affect Q/K only, while values remain
contents. Decoder contents start at zero and learned query positions enter
every layer's Q/K. Encoder/decoder blocks use original post-norm residual
ordering. Class and three-layer sigmoid box heads share across decoder layers.

The full source ResNet50,6/6-layer,D256,8-head,FF2048,100-query,80-class model
has41,575,061 learned and53,120 BN-state scalars across424 learned tensors.
This full128-pixel backward checks their connections, with expected zero
initial derivatives from zero-content self-attention and invariant key biases.
Backbone BN is trainable/moving, rather than pretrained frozen BN. Training
dropout uses the parameter-store RNG; the compact demonstration disables it.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  n::ParameterStore p(17), state(17);
  n::models::DetrConfig c;
  c.image_size = 128;
  c.update_stats = false;
  const auto net = n::models::Detr(
      p, state, n::sin(.13 * n::arange(0, 128 * 128 * 3)).reshape({1, 128, 128, 3}), c, true);
  n::Tensor objective = n::zeros({});
  for (std::size_t k = 0; k < net.logits.size(); ++k)
    objective =
        objective + n::mean(n::square(net.logits[k])) + n::mean(n::square(net.boxes[k]));
  const auto g = n::grad(objective, p.parameters());
  if (p.count() != 41575061 || state.count() != 53120 || g.size() != 424 ||
      net.logits.size() != 6)
    return 1;
  int nonzero = 0;
  for (const auto &v : g) {
    if (!v.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(v)).item()))
      return 1;
    if (n::sum(n::square(v)).item() > 0)
      ++nonzero;
  }
  std::print(
      "Full initialized DETR128: {} learned/{} state scalars,{} decoder outputs,{} defined "
      "finite tensor gradients ({} nonzero). Initial zero-content/invariant-bias derivatives "
      "are expected. No pretraining or benchmark fitting.\n",
      p.count(), state.count(), net.logits.size(), g.size(), nonzero);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Full initialized DETR128: 41575061 learned/53120 state scalars,6 decoder outputs,424 defined finite tensor gradients (417 nonzero). Initial zero-content/invariant-bias derivatives are expected. No pretraining or benchmark fitting.
// result_end

The compact source configuration uses ResNet18/8, a small stem with8x8
memory at64 pixels,D64,four heads,FF128,two encoder/two decoder layers andten
queries/classes. It has357,399 learned and1,200 state scalars. At initialization,
150 of157 tensor gradients are nonzero; zero-content first self-attention and
key-bias invariance explain the others. The parameter and moving-state stores
are warmed before optimizer construction.

The split uses64 fit/16 validation MNIST-derived training scenes(first2048
digits,seed11) and eight test scenes(first512 official test digits,seed22).
Actual input scenes and boxes appear below.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/detr_scenes.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("mnist", (cache / "mnist").string());

  const auto train = n::load_mnist((cache / "mnist").string(), "train");
  n::models::DetectionSceneConfig cfg;
  cfg.scenes = 80;
  cfg.seed = 11;
  const auto scenes = n::models::MakeTensorDetectionScenes(
      n::slice_axis(train.images, 0, 0, 2048), n::slice_axis(train.labels, 0, 0, 2048), cfg);

  std::vector<n::Tensor> boxes(scenes.boxes.begin(), scenes.boxes.begin() + 8);
  const auto preview = n::models::DrawDetectionBoxes(n::slice_axis(scenes.images, 0, 0, 8),
                                                     boxes, {.1, 1., .2});
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(preview, "build/detr_scenes.png", 4, 0., 1., 4, 1., 2);
  std::int64_t objects = 0;
  for (const auto &b : scenes.boxes)
    objects += b.shape()[0];
  std::print("80 generated training/validation scenes; {} accepted digits. Preview: first "
             "eight training scenes with tight green boxes.\n",
             objects);
}
