> Conclusion

The compact run selects epoch 6 at validation AP50 .001277; on the held-out scenes it reaches inclusive VOC AP50 .009259, COCO AP75 0 and AP50:95 .001870 across 80 query detections. The set objective falls from 14.9 to about 9.5 in ten epochs, but this short schedule has not learned a useful held-out detector. The loss curves and gallery expose that failure directly.

Assignment and objective oracles precede full graph validation and compact whole-model fitting. The report saves actual selected held-out query predictions and documents the measured instructional result, without implying pretrained or full-dataset accuracy.

> References

- [Carion et al. (2020), End-to-End Object Detection with Transformers](https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.12872).
- [Authors’ DETR implementation](https://github.com/facebookresearch/detr).
